# The rescaling degeneracy map Vd​ on cusp forms

Definition: `FreyPackage_ModMCarrier_Rescale` (`5a5580ba-bc45-5d78-87e6-3b66d0c19953`), by Claude,
2026-09-05.

Fix natural numbers $R$, $M$, $d$. The module introduces `diagMatInt d`, the integral matrix
$\begin{pmatrix} d & 0 \\ 0 & 1\end{pmatrix}$, and `heckeDiagMatrixQ`, its rational avatar in
$\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q})$ for $d \neq 0$, whose entrywise image under $\mathbb{Q} \to \mathbb{R}$
is the matrix `heckeDiagMatrix d` of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{R})$ already used to define the Hecke
operators. The conjugation lemma `exists_cocycle_rescale` states that if $dR \mid M$ and $\gamma \in
\Gamma_0(M)$, then there is $\delta \in \Gamma_0(R)$ with $\mathrm{diag}(d,1)\,\gamma =
\delta\,\mathrm{diag}(d,1)$; explicitly, for $\gamma = \begin{pmatrix} a & b \\ c & e\end{pmatrix}$
with $c = dRc'$ one takes $\delta = \begin{pmatrix} a & db \\ Rc' & e\end{pmatrix}$, of determinant
$1$ and lower-left entry divisible by $R$. From this, `rescaleSlash_slash` deduces that for $M \neq
0$, $dR \mid M$ and $f : \mathbb{H} \to \mathbb{C}$ invariant under the weight-$k$ slash action of
the image of $\Gamma_0(R)$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{R})$, the function $f \mid_k
\mathrm{diag}(d,1)$ is invariant under the image of $\Gamma_0(M)$; and `rescaleSlash_isZeroAt` shows
that if $f$ is zero at every cusp of $\Gamma_0(R)$ then $f \mid_k \mathrm{diag}(d,1)$ is zero at
every cusp of $\Gamma_0(M)$, the cusp condition being transported because $\mathrm{diag}(d,1)$ is
rational and hence carries $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$-cusps to $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$-cusps.

These three facts, together with holomorphy of a slashed holomorphic function, supply the
invariance, holomorphy and cusp-vanishing fields of `rescaleLin hdRM k`, the $\mathbb{C}$-linear map
$\mathrm{CuspForm}(\Gamma_0(R), k) \to \mathrm{CuspForm}(\Gamma_0(M), k)$ sending $f$ to the
function $f \mid_k \mathrm{heckeDiagMatrix}\ d$, i.e. $\tau \mapsto d^{k-1} f(d\tau)$ in the
determinant-normalised slash action; `coe_rescaleLin_apply` records this formula for the underlying
function. Finally, for an Atkin–Lehner datum $W$ at $(M, q')$, which carries the equation $M = q'
\cdot W.R$ as a field, `q_mul_R_dvd` gives $q' \cdot W.R \mid M$ and `rescaleLinAL W k` is the
resulting map $\mathrm{CuspForm}(\Gamma_0(W.R), k) \to \mathrm{CuspForm}(\Gamma_0(M), k)$.

**Relation to Mathlib.** Mathlib provides the weight-$k$ slash action on functions on $\mathbb{H}$,
the spaces `CuspForm` for arithmetic subgroups of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{R})$ and the cusp
predicates used here; the degeneracy map $V_d$ between levels, and the diagonal matrix
`heckeDiagMatrix` it is built from, are the project's own.

**Where it is used.** The map $V_{q'}$ attached to an Atkin–Lehner datum is one of the two
degeneracy maps $S_k(\Gamma_0(R)) \to S_k(\Gamma_0(q'R))$, the other being the level inclusion; the
pair is the source of the level-raising argument, where joint injectivity modulo a maximal ideal of
the Hecke algebra is Ihara's lemma.

